[[File:SepAAT-TCWIV.png|thumb|300px|An [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|Armored Assault Tank]] used by the Confederacy of Independent Systems.]]
{{Quote|Tanks. Is that the best they can throw at us?|Rys, during the Ambush on Rugosa|audio=Rys-Tanks.flac|<ref name="Ambush">{{TCW|Ambush}}</ref>}}
'''Tanks''' were [[armored cavalry]] [[ground assault vehicle]]s that were capable of extreme mobility thanks to their tracks, legs, wheels or a [[repulsorlift]]. Used by [[Army|armies]] as part of [[armored cavalry]] units, they were designed for front-line combat as well as intimidation. They typically boasted large [[laser cannon]]s mounted on turrets or other powerful anti-vehicle weaponry, and were heavily [[armor]]ed to protect the [[troop]]s operating the weapons and the propulsion systems inside.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

The [[pirate]] [[Hondo Ohnaka]], leader of the [[Ohnaka Gang]], maintained a philosophy of both speaking softly and driving a large tank.<ref name="BH">{{TCW|Bounty Hunters (episode)}}</ref> The [[Trade Federation]],<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]],<ref name="Hailfire Droid">{{Databank|hailfire-droid|Hailfire Droid}}</ref> [[Corporate Alliance]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> [[Umbaran Militia]],<ref name="Umbaran Hover Tank Databank">{{Databank|umbran-hover-tank|Umbaran Hover Tank}}</ref> [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> and [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] all manufactured or deployed tanks in some capacity.<ref name="FA">''[[Star Wars: Force Arena]]''</ref>

